From: Arctic <arctic@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Pictures of menu items in the columns of Windows 11.

A picture of 32 bits with alpha is blended over its item, as Windows does
since Vista: not inverted under the pointer, faded when the item is grayed.
A Windows 11 popup whose items have pictures lays them out as Windows 11's
context menus do: a column for check marks only while one is checked, the
pictures centred in a column of their own, the text after them.
